ng the kin byd  came out with the u1 in march of 2016.  the yuan was offered as a compact  crossover suv that was offered as a  hybrid and as a full ev  the hybrid version cost between thirty  two thousand dollars and thirty eight  thousand dollars so still under that 40k  mark both the can and yuan were solid  vehicles but by far their biggest jump  forward came with the han which was  released in july of 2020.  the haunt instantly sticks out as a  modern dv with its sleek design but not  only does it look good it's also quite  affordable the standard range comes with  314 miles of range and only costs 33 730  you can also get the extended range  which comes with 376 miles of range and  cost 36 540  byd quickly followed up the han with  this leak suv called the song in  september of 2020. the song also boasts  a range above 300 miles and comes in  under 40k  so though by these sales have remained  stagnant for a decade i think we'd agree  that byd is a completely different  company today than they were in 2010.  as for byd today i believe that they're  on the cusp of a massive boom in july  the han crossed 100 000 deliveries and i  don't really see anything stopping them  from reaching millions  also byd formed a partnership with  toyota two years ago originally it  seemed like they were just going to  manufacture some models together but  they actually ended up creating a new  car company called byd toyota in april  of 2020.  it's not clear when they launched their  first car but it should be within the  next few years as nine of them are new  to the car business  in terms of international expansion byd  does have some presence within latin  america and some scandinavian countries  but the vast majority of their business  comes from china  wang does eventually want to spend more  time on the western market with this  long-term goal of being 20 to 30 percent  of sales coming from outside china but  even if that doesn't materialize it's  not that big of a deal given